---
import AplusPage from '../../layouts/AplusPage.astro';
---
<AplusPage title="Case Study | PHI Scrubber" eyebrow="Case study" heading="PHI scrubber for safer healthcare building." intro="A prototype pattern for making examples, demos, and internal review safer before teams share work across tools.">
  <section class="aplus-screen-stack" aria-label="PHI scrubber workflow">
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">Current state</p>
      <h2>Healthcare demos need realism, but private context creates risk.</h2>
      <p>The Slack throughline is practical: we need worked examples, screenshots, and demos that people can trust without leaking sensitive patient, practice, or guest information.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="aplus-kicker">Future state</p>
      <h2>Demo-safe artifacts let Healthcare Engineers teach in public.</h2>
      <p>The scrubber path turns risky raw material into synthetic examples, human-reviewed notes, and reusable assets for office hours, masterclasses, Slack handoffs, and retained implementation.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-flywheel-strip" aria-label="PHI scrubber outputs">
    <span>Synthetic examples</span>
    <span>Human review</span>
    <span>Demo-safe artifacts</span>
    <span>Slack handoff</span>
    <span>Retainer build</span>
  </section>
  <section class="aplus-content-grid">
    <article><h2>The problem</h2><p>Builders need realistic data and screenshots, but healthcare workflows carry privacy risk.</p></article>
    <article><h2>The MVP</h2><p>A workflow that detects sensitive details, asks for review, and produces safer artifacts for collaboration.</p></article>
    <article><h2>The offer fit</h2><p>Members learn the pattern; retained teams can adapt it for their own operational stack.</p></article>
  </section>
</AplusPage>
